     1	# Capture and annotate a screenshot
     2	
     3	Choose an area, add annotations, and review the result in the composer before sending.
     4	
     5	## Capture from a conversation
     6	
     7	1. Open a conversation and expand the composer tools if they are collapsed.
     8	2. Open **Screenshot** and choose the capture option, including hiding Mesh-Talk first if desired.
     9	3. Follow any operating-system permission or capture prompt.
    10	4. Select an area in the editor. Adjust its bounds and use the available drawing, text or mosaic tools as needed.
    11	5. Confirm the edit to copy the cropped, annotated image to the clipboard and put it in the composer. Review the intended conversation and press **Enter** or choose **Send** when ready.
    12	
    13	Enter also sends a staged screenshot if capture returns focus to the page background. Shift+Enter and input-method confirmation do not send it; focused controls and open dialogs keep their own keyboard behavior.
    14	
    15	Confirming an edit does not send it immediately. Cancel closes the editor without changing the clipboard or sending a screenshot. If clipboard copying fails, the editor keeps your selection and annotations so you can retry confirmation. If sending fails, review the retained draft and error before retrying.
    16	
    17	## Keyboard shortcuts
    18	
    19	Open **Settings → Shortcuts** to change the two capture bindings, clear a binding
    20	or restore defaults. Initially, **Capture screen** uses Ctrl+Shift+X and **Hide
    21	window & capture** uses Ctrl+Alt+Shift+X. On macOS use Command in place of Ctrl
    22	and Option in place of Alt. Shortcuts work inside Mesh-Talk by default. Enable
    23	**Use screenshot shortcuts globally** to activate them while using another app;
    24	Mesh-Talk must remain running and unlocked. If a global shortcut is unavailable,
    25	choose another binding or release it in the other app, then retry. Linux global
    26	shortcuts require native X11; Wayland supports application shortcuts.
    27	
    28	Hover over the screenshot entry or an editor icon to see its current shortcut.
    29	Capture bindings are saved only on this device. Without a writable conversation,
    30	activation shows the app and asks you to select a conversation first.
    31	
    32	| Editor action | Key |
    33	| --- | --- |
    34	| Select an area | V |
    35	| Rectangle | R |
    36	| Ellipse | O |
    37	| Arrow | A |
    38	| Draw | P |
    39	| Mosaic | M |
    40	| Text | T |
    12	//!
    13	//! Modeled on the device-pairing wire ([`super::pairing`]): a magic-prefixed, bincode frame
    14	//! peeked off the first frame of a connection in `serve_connection`, distinct from a sync wire.
    15	
    16	use super::*;
    17	use crate::discovery::roster::UserId;
    18	use crate::node::session::SessionError;
    19	use crate::node::wire::{frame, unframe};
    20	use crate::transport::SecureChannel;
    21	use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
    22	use tokio::net::TcpStream;
    23	
    24	const CALL_MAGIC: &[u8] = b"MTCS1";
    25	
    26	/// The wire form: an opaque application payload (the app's JSON — call id, kind, SDP). The
    27	/// node neither parses nor persists it; it is a dumb, authenticated pipe for the frontend's
    28	/// WebRTC negotiation. Uses the shared magic-frame helper ([`crate::node::wire`]).
    29	#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
    30	pub struct CallSignal {
    31	    pub payload: Vec<u8>,
    32	}
    33	
    34	impl CallSignal {
    35	    pub fn encode(&self) -> Vec<u8> {
    36	        frame(CALL_MAGIC, self)
    37	    }
    38	
    39	    pub fn decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<Self> {
    40	        unframe(CALL_MAGIC, bytes)
    41	    }
    42	}
    43	
    44	/// A received call signal, surfaced live to the app. `from` is the AUTHENTICATED sender
    45	/// device (taken from the Noise channel), never a self-asserted wire field.
    46	#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
    47	pub struct ReceivedCallSignal {
    48	    pub from: UserId,
    49	    pub payload: Vec<u8>,
    50	}
    51	
    52	impl Node {
    53	    /// Send an opaque call-signaling `payload` to a specific device `target_user_id`, right
    54	    /// now, over a fresh authenticated Noise channel. Ephemeral: nothing is appended to the
    55	    /// event log, and there is NO post-office fallback — a live call requires both devices
    56	    /// online, so this errors if the peer is unknown or unreachable.
    57	    ///
    58	    /// Always device-addressed (a call rings one device), never an account fan-out.
    59	    pub async fn send_call_signal(
    60	        &self,
    61	        target_user_id: &str,
    62	        payload: &[u8],
    63	    ) -> Result<(), NodeError> {
    64	        self.send_call_signal_if(target_user_id, payload, |commit| commit())
    65	            .await
    66	    }
    67	
    68	    /// Authorize frame encryption after dial and policy waits, before any payload write.
    69	    pub async fn send_call_signal_if(
    70	        &self,
    71	        target_user_id: &str,
    72	        payload: &[u8],
    73	        mut authorize: impl FnMut(&mut dyn FnMut() -> Result<(), NodeError>) -> Result<(), NodeError>
    74	        + Send,
    75	    ) -> Result<(), NodeError> {
    76	        authorize(&mut || Ok(()))?;
    77	        let peer = self
    78	            .routing_peer(target_user_id)
    79	            .ok_or_else(|| NodeError::UnknownPeer(target_user_id.to_string()))?;
    80	        if !self.known_account_allowed(&peer.public) {
    81	            return Err(NodeError::Session(SessionError::Transport(
    82	                crate::transport::TransportError::AdmissionDenied,
    83	            )));
    84	        }
    85	        let frame = CallSignal {
    86	            payload: payload.to_vec(),
    87	        }
    88	        .encode();
    89	        let mut channel = self
    90	            .privacy_dial_interactive(peer.addr, &peer.public)
    91	            .await
    92	            .map_err(SessionError::Transport)
    93	            .map_err(NodeError::Session)?;
    94	        channel
    95	            .send_if(&frame, |commit| {
    96	                authorize(&mut || {
    97	                    commit()
    98	                        .map_err(SessionError::Transport)
    99	                        .map_err(NodeError::Session)
   100	                })
   101	                .map_err(|error| match error {
   102	                    NodeError::Session(SessionError::Transport(error)) => error,
   103	                    _ => crate::transport::TransportError::AdmissionDenied,
   104	                })
   105	            })
   106	            .await
   107	            .map_err(SessionError::Transport)
   108	            .map_err(NodeError::Session)?;
   109	        Ok(())
   110	    }

